# NHL-Data scheduled collection. Install with:  crontab -e  (append these lines)
#
# Times are local (America/New_York on this machine), so they are ET. Paths must be
# absolute: cron has no shell profile and does not expand ~. Every wrapper sources
# scripts/_common.sh (venv, .env, a mkdir lock, a timeout) and prints a `=== name ts ===`
# header per run so log readers (OpsView) can find the last run.
#
# Cadence rationale: only line/report *changes* are stored, so a poll where nothing moved
# writes nothing. Dense, uniform polling is therefore nearly free, while a missed
# closing line can never be recovered. Two layers per source:
#   * a uniform baseline around the clock (odds) or across the news day (lineups);
#   * a pregame window (--window 90): fires every 5 minutes but only polls when a game
#     starts within 90 minutes, which is what captures the close and confirmed starters.

REPO=/Users/tommywinfield/GitRepos/NHL-Data

# --- Odds: LowVig, 4Casters, ESPN books ------------------------------------------------
*/15 * * * *     $REPO/scripts/poll.sh odds                   >> $REPO/logs/poll_odds.log 2>&1
2-57/5 * * * *   $REPO/scripts/poll.sh odds --window 90       >> $REPO/logs/poll_odds.log 2>&1

# --- Starting goalies + injuries (DailyFaceoff, ESPN) ----------------------------------
# News breaks from morning skate (~10-11am) to warmups; nothing useful overnight.
7-52/15 8-23 * * *  $REPO/scripts/poll.sh goalies,injuries             >> $REPO/logs/poll_lineups.log 2>&1
4-59/5 * * * *      $REPO/scripts/poll.sh goalies,injuries --window 90 >> $REPO/logs/poll_lineups.log 2>&1

# --- Line combinations (32 team pages at 0.5 req/s, ~65 s) -----------------------------
11 8-23 * * *      $REPO/scripts/poll.sh lines              >> $REPO/logs/poll_lines.log 2>&1
26,41,56 * * * *   $REPO/scripts/poll.sh lines --window 90  >> $REPO/logs/poll_lines.log 2>&1

# --- Nightly model/data refresh ---------------------------------------------------------
30 6 * * *  $REPO/scripts/nightly.sh  >> $REPO/logs/nightly.log 2>&1
